Source code. 

Material.py
	Holds information about materials, such as their lattice parameters, atomic form factors, etc

Experiment.py
	holds all general information about the experiment in a way that is easily programmable for future iterating 

Crystal.py
	Crystal structure and associated reciprocal lattice information 
	Has the ability to generate a grain with a randomized size, strain, and orientation. 

Ewald
	Receives grain data. Projects points onto the detector. Calculates those points’ 2theta, and sends information about the grain to the detector. 
	

Detector.py
	Receives data from Ewald and projects it onto the detector. 

Experimental broadening.py
	Looks at all information on the detector and creates Gaussian distributions at those spots

Instrumental broadening.py
	Applies a general broadening to all points. 
	[Currently named “point on detector]]
